  "problem": "HCUP, MEPS and AHA lacked evidence-backed access workflows. Public MEPS files could be labeled restricted solely because another MEPS product is restricted. AHA terms could be inferred. Undocumented fees or eligibility could be guessed. USHSO could collect a user's eligibility or credentials. An agent could claim a successful restricted-data download. Catalog, license and payload access could collapse into one dimension. Sealed packages/identity/src could be edited.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Access workflows live in packages/connectors/source-registry/access-workflows.mjs because packages/identity is WP7-sealed. Public MEPS files remain public_download even when a sibling MEPS product is restricted. AHA terms remain unknown unless cited. Each workflow step cites a source. Undocumented fees or eligibility remain unknown. USHSO never collects eligibility or credentials. An agent can explain the next legitimate step and cannot claim a successful restricted-data download. Catalog, license and payload access remain separate. Sealed identity src and named-source-registry are unchanged. Last-good generation live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420 is unchanged.",
